WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.472
Given the rewards, an epsilon optimal expert
policy, and the batch data,

00:00:04.552 --> 00:00:09.909
we use the closed form Bellman equations to write
constraints that demand the value of

00:00:09.989 --> 00:00:14.651
actions the expert takes exceed the value of
actions the expert never took.

00:00:14.731 --> 00:00:20.973
Any dynamics satisfying these constraints recovers
what we call the expert's epsilon ball structure.

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:26.853
We then place a Dirichlet multinomial posterior
over the dynamics and use rejection sampling,

00:00:26.933 --> 00:00:30.267
keeping only the samples that satisfy the constraints.

00:00:30.347 --> 00:00:35.578
The surviving samples form a clipped posterior that
respects the expert's knowledge.

00:00:35.658 --> 00:00:40.952
Separate constraint sets handle a fully optimal
expert and a partially uncertain one,

00:00:41.032 --> 00:00:47.970
with a tunable slack term that enforces the
structure even where action non linearity would otherwise break it.
